            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Hindi for an inscription (on stone), then the Hindi for remains."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: पूर्वज",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "पूर्वज — pūrvaj — \"an ancestor\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "हमारे पूर्वज सौ साल पहले इस गाँव में आए। hamāre pūrvaj sau sāl pahle is gā̃v meṁ āe. Our ancestors came to this village a hundred years ago."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "पूर्वज (pūrvaj) is Sanskrit pūrvaja, \"born before\" (Monier-Williams), pūrva, earlier, and -ja, born: those who came before us."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
